WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.467
-Jimmy Fallon.
-That's a stud right there.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:03.534
-Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.167
-Morris Chestnut,
welcome to the show, bud.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:06.100
-Thank you, man. Thank you.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.834
-I want to get into "Best Man,"

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:10.067
but before we even get into
that, I want to talk about this.

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:13.100
You were the 1998 winner
of the Madden Bowl.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.133
-Yes, I was. I was.

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.767
-We gave out
a Nintendo Switch earlier,

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.567
so I want to talk
to you about gaming.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.067
How did you win this?
I know what this thing is.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:23.300
Do you want to tell everyone
what this is?

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.033
-So, the Madden Bowl
was every Super Bowl.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:28.167
"John Madden Football"
was a video game.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.901
So every year at the Super Bowl,
they would have

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:33.100
this huge tournament where
actors, celebrities,

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.734
players would play in
a tournament to see who is

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.434
the Super Bowl champion,
or the Madden Bowl champion.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:38.534
-I remember this.
-Yes.

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:39.934
-And you won it?
-And I won it, yes, yes.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:42.901
-[ Cheers and applause ]
I was very proud of that moment.

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:44.234
-You should be proud of that.

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:47.501
-That was my highest honor.
-Oh, please.

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.601
But how did you --
Did you game all the time?

00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:51.667
-Oh, yeah, oh, no.
So I have a group of friends,

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.200
and we used to play
all the time.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.534
It was something that we really
took seriously.

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:57.667
It wasn't just
a video game to us.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.133
It was like --
It was like chess.

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:02.934
It was an elevated chess match,
and we really took it seriously.

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:05.267
-I got into this a little bit
and did a little research.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:08.133
You went out to -- You used to
go to Vegas and do tournaments?

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.100
-Yeah, so, yeah.
It was funny too.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.634
So, yes.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:12.968
I was a grown man
playing video games

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:14.767
and going to tournaments, right?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:18.534
-Here's the funny thing, because
one year it was in Miami.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:21.000
And so I went to this tournament
in Miami.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.200
It was a room full of people.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.634
I think it was like 200 players
or whatever.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:26.400
And Tyrese was staying
in the same hotel.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.801
And so he heard that I was
there, so he came down.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.567
And he saw me,
and he's like, "Yo."

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:33.501
He just saw me in the room.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.067
He said, "Yo, Morris, what's up?
What's good?

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:38.000
You here doing a movie?
What are you doing? Some press?"

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.634
I said, "No."
I said, "I'm in the tournament.

00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:41.701
I'm in this Madden tournament."

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.300
And he looked at me
kind of confused.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.434
He's like, "You came from L.A.
to Miami to play a video game?"

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:48.901
-[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. That's exactly right.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.601
-And I was like, "Yeah, yeah."

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.033
So that's what it was.
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:55.067
-He was like, "Oh, okay."
But, yeah, it was funny.

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:58.100
-Well, actually,
we have video of you.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.267
-Oh, you do?

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:02.868
-Of winning, you winning
the 1998 Madden Bowl.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:05.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.634
Take a look at this.

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:11.167
-We are here with the champion
of the Madden Bowl '98,

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.434
Mr. Morris --
-Chestnut, that's right.

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.467
Morris Chestnut.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.234
-Oh, touchdown!

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:19.267
-I got a few guys I play with
back home.

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:20.801
We call ourselves
the Federation.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.400
Federation, Yeah!

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.801
-I lost though.
But you know what?

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.634
I lost to one of the best people
in here though.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.334
-Who'd you lose to?
-Morris Chestnut.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.133
-There you go. Come on.
-[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.934
Coolio.
-Late, great Coolio.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:33.033
Late, great Coolio.
-Love Coolio.

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:34.100
-Yeah, no, that was great.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.133
That was a good time, man.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.234
It was hype. It was hype.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:37.534
-Look at how hyped up
you were there.

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:38.734
You were like, "Yeah, what's up,
Federation?!"

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:40.834
-Because people don't
understand.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:43.901
They didn't understand the level
of the intensity of this.

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.200
This is bragging rights.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.000
I mean, we literally --
you know, we would bet

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.634
thousands of dollars on games.

00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.133
We'd say cash on the console.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.968
So it was really --
it was really a big thing.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.400
-And you had a name
for your group?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.701
-Yeah, so our group was called
the Federation.

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:58.501
And I don't really remember how
we got that name,

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.968
but we all had little nicknames
inside the Federation.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:03.400
So whenever we went somewhere,
like, we were playing

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.300
against another group of
whatever their name was.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.901
-You'd just yell "Federation."
-Federation, yeah.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.400
-I was like,
"Why's he yelling 'Federation'?"

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.667
-One year we went up north

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:14.834
and we played against
a headbusters crew.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.234
So it was just a whole bunch of
crew type -- crew versus crew.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:21.434
It was some real, like --
it was real edgy,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.000
gang-type stuff,
you know what I mean?

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.067
-[ Laughter ]
-No, no. It was not that.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.400
No, it wasn't.
-No, it wasn't that.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.200
-That is an honor for you,
obviously, of course.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.834
But you're on the Walk of Fame,
the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:34.701
That is a real --
-Yes, oh, yes.

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.667
-Look at that.
-Oh, thank you. Yes.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:40.467
-[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. Thank you.

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:42.901
-And you wanted this March 23rd.

00:03:42.901 --> 00:03:44.434
-Yes, yes.

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:46.934
-You actually said, "Hey, can
I -- I'm honored to get this.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.133
Can I move it to March 23rd?"

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.100
Because it was
a very specific date for you.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:53.000
-It was a specific date.
So, one day my mother just came

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.400
and she said, "Hey, you
should -- you know,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.534
you need to be on the Hall of
Fame -- the Walk of Fame."

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.868
I was like, "Ah, I don't really
think about that.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.667
I'm just trying to go from job
to job and keep moving."

00:03:59.667 --> 00:04:01.767
She goes,
"No, I want you to get your star

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.901
on the Hollywood Walk of Fame."
So she called my publicist

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.334
and activated my publicist

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.667
and my wife and they went out
and they got it done.

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:09.868
So, I said, you know,
as a tribute to her,

00:04:09.868 --> 00:04:12.000
I want it to be given to me
on her birthday.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.200
So I selected March 23rd
is when I got my --

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.801
[ Applause ]

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.834
-And Mom is there.
-And that's Mom. That's her.

00:04:17.834 --> 00:04:19.334
-Mom was right there.
There's Mom. Come on.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:20.767
-It was done on her birthday.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:23.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.267
-How cute is that?

00:04:24.267 --> 00:04:25.701
-Yeah, done on her birthday.

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:28.167
-What would we be
without our moms?

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:29.167
-Oh, without a doubt.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:30.534
-No, nothing.
-Nothing.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:33.300
-I want to talk about "The Best
Man: The Final Chapters."

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.567
Where is your character now?

00:04:35.567 --> 00:04:36.601
Where do we find him?

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.601
-So, we last left my character,

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:40.167
his wife passed away
in the movie.

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:43.000
So now, when this version
opens up,

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.100
he's kind of really
trying to find himself.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:49.400
And he's trying to find himself
by trying to take away the pain.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.534
And in all seriousness,
he's really just trying to

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:54.667
not feel the pain
of losing his wife.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.467
So he's kind of going around
doing a few things.

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:59.634
-It's dramatic, but it's also
very funny as well.

00:04:59.634 --> 00:05:01.234
-It's fun, yes, and funny, yes.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.834
-Yeah. Well, you also know
the cast for years.

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:05.467
-Oh, yeah. Oh, no, yeah, we've
been working together --

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:08.234
I mean, the original
we did in 1999.

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:09.634
-Is that right?
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:10.801
I was 10 years old back then.

00:05:10.801 --> 00:05:12.801
So, if you guys are
doing the math...

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:15.300
-Yeah, but you were
Madden Bowl champ.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.501
So, hello! Come on.
-But I was Madden Bowl champion.

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:17.634
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:05:17.634 --> 00:05:18.834
Federation!

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:19.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:21.334
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:24.334
Here's Morris Chestnut in "The
Best Man: The Final Chapters."

00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:25.934
Take a look at this.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:28.534
-We would have celebrated
our 20th.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:38.133
You know, it's the -- it's the
"what ifs" that always haunt me.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.000
What if you were still here?

00:05:46.601 --> 00:05:48.334
What would you have done?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.901
I know you would have
loved our son.

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:57.634
[ Sighs ]

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:00.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.667 --> 00:06:01.968
-It gets a little emotional.

00:06:01.968 --> 00:06:03.300
-Come on, buddy.
-It gets a little emotional.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.634
Gets a little emotional.
-It's a pleasure.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:05.601
-Thank you for having me, man.
I appreciate it.

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:06.901
-Morris Chestnut, everybody.

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:08.567
"The Best Man:
The Final Chapters"

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:11.133
begins streaming on Peacock
December 22nd.

